Z||000000||KnightRyder31||07-14-2000||12:09 AM||||For some reason, when I first start up my car, I hear this strange ticking noise comeing form the engine. Its not every time I start it, but quite often. My friend told me it was my rocker's makeing that noise...I dont know. The ticking sound goes away after a couple of minutes of driveing. By the way, I own a 84 4cyl. auto, Coupe.<BR>Knight-||||reg||9
Z||000001||Standard||07-14-2000||01:44 AM||||That's your hydraulic lifters sticking.  Not too serious of a problem, and not too hard to fix.  go to <A HREF="http://members.xoom.com/_XMCM/fierov6/OSG/lifters.html" TARGET=_blank>Fiero OSG Lifter Info</A>  Lot's of information in there.<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 147,000 miles and counting!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
